export const FAQ=[
['When is the best time to visit Egypt?','October to April. Days are warm and dry, ideal for Cairo, Luxor and Aswan. Summer (June to August) passes 40°C in Upper Egypt, though the Red Sea coast stays pleasant for beach and diving trips.'],
['How many days do I need?','7 to 8 days covers Cairo, Giza and a 3 or 4-night Nile cruise. Add 3 to 4 days for the Red Sea, or 2 to 3 for the Western Desert or Alexandria.'],
['Is the Grand Egyptian Museum open?','Yes. It opened fully in November 2025 next to the Giza Pyramids. Entry is by timed ticket, and from 1 November 2026 the foreign adult ticket is EGP 1,830.'],
['What currency is used, and can I pay by card?','The Egyptian pound (EGP). Cards work in hotels, malls and most restaurants. Carry some cash for tips, small shops and taxis. ATMs are common in cities.'],
['How does tipping (baksheesh) work?','Tipping is expected. Typical amounts: 10% in restaurants if service is not included, EGP 20–50 for porters and bathroom attendants, and USD 5–10 per day for guides and drivers on tours.'],
['Is Egypt safe for tourists?','The main tourist areas (Cairo, Giza, Luxor, Aswan, Red Sea resorts) are heavily visited and policed, with a dedicated Tourist Police. Check your government’s travel advice for areas to avoid, such as parts of North Sinai and border zones.'],
['What should I wear?','Light, loose clothes that cover shoulders and knees in cities and at religious sites. Women need a scarf for mosques. Swimwear is fine at resorts and beaches.'],
['Can I drink tap water?','Drink bottled or filtered water. Hotels and cruise ships provide it.'],
['Which plugs and voltage?','220V, 50Hz. Type C and F (European two-pin) sockets.'],
['Is Uber available?','Uber and Careem run in Cairo, Giza and Alexandria. In Luxor, Aswan and resort towns, book transfers or agree a taxi fare first.'],
['Can I fly a drone?','No. Drones are banned without a special permit and are confiscated at customs.'],
['What happens during Ramadan?','Sites stay open, often with shorter hours. Many restaurants close during the day and open for iftar at sunset. Eating in public during daylight is best avoided.'],
['How long is a Nile cruise?','3 nights (Aswan to Luxor), 4 nights (Luxor to Aswan) or 7 nights round trip. Dahabiya sailing boats usually take 4 to 5 nights.'],
['Do I need travel insurance?','It is not required for entry, but recommended, especially for diving, ballooning and desert trips.']
];
